  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Louisiana recorded $4.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buying agency with $2.4B, followed by the Department of Defense with $1.5B. Contracting activity has produced 20,876 awards so far, with an average award size of $225K. Obligations are down 1.2% year over year. Ship Building and Repairing is the largest industry by obligations at $2.5B, reflecting the scale of maritime and shipbuilding work in the state. BOLLINGER SHIPYARDS LOCKPORT, L.L.C. is the top vendor with $2.2B in obligations, well ahead of other suppliers. Historic year comparisons show FY25 at $4.8B and FY24 at $3.9B, situating FY26 to date within recent annual variation. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is driving the concentration of federal obligations in Louisiana?",
        "body": "Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $2.5B, which is the single largest industry concentration. The Department of Homeland Security contributes $2.4B and the Department of Defense contributes $1.5B, concentrating buying power in maritime and defense-related work."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are vendors and agencies in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "BOLLINGER SHIPYARDS LOCKPORT, L.L.C. holds $2.2B in obligations, making the vendor landscape highly concentrated at the top. The top two agencies together account for $3.9B in obligations, which dominates the $4.7B total."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Louisiana?",
      "a": "The state of Louisiana receives $4.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Louisiana has 20,876 awards so far and an average award size of $225K. Obligations are down 1.2% year over year, and the largest industry by obligations is Ship Building and Repairing at $2.5B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Louisiana?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security awards the most contracts in Louisiana with $2.4B. The Department of Defense is the second largest buyer with $1.5B, followed by the Department of Energy with $263M and the Department of Agriculture with $94.6M."
    },
